--- body ---
## Context
Audit after the 0116 merge surfaced 7 code-quality items: file/parse
redundancy in command implementations, and naming leftovers from
historical refactors.

## File-read / parse redundancy
1. `cmdClose` reads the ticket file three times (close.go:73, 79, 105):
   one `ReadFile` plus two `parseErg` calls on the same path.
2. `removeBlockedByRef` parses each candidate file, then re-reads the
   same bytes for rewriting (close.go:128, 147).
3. `cmdArchive` double-parses every target: `loadErgs` walks the
   directory once (archive.go:57), then `parseErg` is called again on
   the chosen ticket (archive.go:93, 109).
4. `globLocalIDs` re-reads the directory once per file when
   `cmdValidate` is invoked with multiple files from the same dir —
   validate.go:247, called from cmdValidate at validate.go:320.

For each: refactor to read/parse once and pass the parsed `Erg` down.

## Naming leftovers
5. `sortedKeys2` (erg.go:366): the trailing "2" is a leftover from a
   prior refactor; the original `sortedKeys` is gone. Rename to
   `sortedKeys`.
6. `commandOrder` (helptext.go:4) + `helpText` (helptext.go:14) are
   parallel structures listing the same 12 commands. Collapse to a
   single ordered struct keeping per-command help inline.

## Re-litigation deliberately deferred
7. `Line` type alias (erg.go:11): audit flagged that as a pure alias
   it adds no type safety, only documentation. Decision was made in
   0116 to keep it for godoc/IDE intent signal. NOT changing here;
   noting for record.

## Actions
1. For each redundancy item (1-4), trace the call paths and propose a
   minimal-touch refactor in the PR description. Implement; verify
   `make test` passes and behavior is unchanged.
2. Rename `sortedKeys2` → `sortedKeys` (mechanical).
3. Collapse `commandOrder` + `helpText` into one ordered structure
   in helptext.go. Update consumers in main.go.

## Out of scope
- Defer-to-0117 items: `ParseDiagnostics` struct + parallel slice
  plumbing through loadErgs/validateAll/check; headerCounts +
  repeatedSeen maps used during parse.
- Defer-to-0118 items: `BlockedByRefs()` accessor re-parsing across
  5+ sites; `detectCycles` re-parsing after `validateErg`;
  `removeBlockedByLine` raw-string ref matching.
- `IsForge` inlining: minor; one call site. Defer (or skip).

## Exit criteria
- All 6 items (1-6) addressed.
- `make test` passes.
- No behaviour change visible to users; reduced syscall and parse
  count verifiable by inspection.
